      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Alfinkedisi",
      "description": "Mount Ida, or Mount Ida, is a mountain located in the north of Edremit Bay between Çanakkale and Balıkesir provinces. The highest peak of the main Kaz Mountain, which has three hills (Babadağ in the north, Karataş Hill in the middle, Sarıkız Hill in the south) is Karataş Hill, the highest peak of which is 1774 meters. is\nKazdağı was called \"Ida\" in ancient times and hosted many important events. It takes place in the mythology that the name was given to Ida by Cretan sailors to refer to Mount Ida in Crete, where Zeus was born. Therefore, the mountain has an important place in Greek mythology.\n\nIn Homer's epic Iliad, it is mentioned as \"a thousand springs Ida\". In Homer's Iliad, he often mentions Mount Ida as \"the mother of wild animals with abundant springs\". Legend has it that the famous beauty contest that led to the Trojan War, in which Hera, Aphrodite and Athena participated, was held here, the gods watched the Trojan War from here and Aphrodite fell in love for the first time here.",
